      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(qa-lab): preserve emoji in Matrix timeout diagnostics",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nMatrix QA tool-progress timeout diagnostics shorten observed event bodies to a 240-code-unit preview. When an emoji crossed the existing raw `slice(0, 237)` boundary, the diagnostic could contain an isolated UTF-16 surrogate and render a replacement character in UTF-8 failure logs.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe shared `truncateUtf16Safe` helper now preserves complete code points while retaining the existing preview budget and suffix. Both preview-wait and final-wait diagnostics use the same formatter.\n\n## User Impact\n\nMatrix QA timeout failures keep valid, actionable Unicode evidence when observed messages contain emoji at the truncation boundary.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/qa-lab/src/live-transports/matrix/scenarios/scenario-runtime-tool-progress-diagnostics.test.ts` (2 tests passed on Node 24.15.0)\n- Added exact-boundary regression coverage for both exported timeout builders, including lone-surrogate and UTF-8 replacement checks.\n- Targeted `oxfmt`, `oxlint`, and `git diff --check` passed.\n- Pre-commit autoreview: clean, no actionable findings (0.85 confidence).\n",
        "branch": "fix/matrix-tool-progress-diagnostics-utf16-20260717",
